WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.920
Is "Renfield" going to get your blood&nbsp;
pounding when it drops in theaters on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:11.100
April 14? Or does it just suck? Here's what the&nbsp;
critics think about the upcoming horror-comedy.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.520
Nicolas Cage is returning to&nbsp;
the big screen this month as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.900
one of the most iconic fictional&nbsp;
characters of all time: Dracula.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:24.840
The Oscar winner stars alongside Nicolas Hoult&nbsp;
in "Renfield," the new film from "The Tomorrow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:30.900
War" director Chris McKay. Based on an original&nbsp;
idea by "Walking Dead" creator Robert Kirkman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:37.320
the film follows Hoult's Renfield, the longtime&nbsp;
henchman of Cage's Dracula, as he tries to start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:43.200
a new life for himself away from his bloodthirsty&nbsp;
boss. As its tongue-in-cheek premise suggests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:49.200
the first "Renfield" trailers have sold the film&nbsp;
as a bloody but lighthearted horror comedy that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.060
perhaps more than anything else, will give Cage&nbsp;
the chance to chew up the scenery once again.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:59.580
Now, ahead of the film's forthcoming April&nbsp;
14 release, the first reviews for "Renfield"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.620
are starting to roll in. While an overall&nbsp;
critical consensus has yet to be cemented,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.480
the early buzz for "Renfield" seems to be&nbsp;
mostly positive right now. That isn't to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.760
say that the early reviews for the film have been&nbsp;
overwhelmingly glowing. As is usually the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.100
some critics have taken to "Renfield" far&nbsp;
more easily than others. Consequence critic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:25.320
Liz Shannon Miller, for instance, gave the&nbsp;
film a B+ score in their review, writing,

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.400
"'Renfield' knows exactly what it wants&nbsp;
to achieve and does so effectively."

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.620
Miller isn't the only critic that enjoyed&nbsp;
"Renfield." In fact, of the film's first 25&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:40.380
Rotten Tomatoes reviews as of the making of this&nbsp;
video, only five are negative. While each critic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:45.600
has offered their own takeaways from the new&nbsp;
horror comedy, those who enjoyed "Renfield" have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.640
repeatedly emphasized the film's combination&nbsp;
of gory violence and chaotic sense of humor.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.520
Maggie Boccella praised the film's horror-comedy&nbsp;
tone in their review for Collider, noting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.160
it has more in common with genre classics like&nbsp;
1981's "An American Werewolf in London" than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:07.020
it does any of its scarier vampire movie&nbsp;
predecessors. Boccella went on to write,

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.540
"Ultimately ['Renfield' is] fun primarily because&nbsp;
it doesn't commit too hard to any one thing."

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.820
Moviegoers will likely be delighted to hear that,&nbsp;
in addition to the film's comic horror spirit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.860
Nicolas Cage's performance as Dracula&nbsp;
has been heavily praised. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.880
the trailers that have been released for&nbsp;
"Renfield" have all suggested that Cage's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.960
performance in it will be one of his&nbsp;
most unabashedly over-the-top in years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.380
and it sounds like the actor has&nbsp;
more than delivered on that front.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.540
"I am dracula."

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.040
In their review of the film for The Playlist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.800
Matthew Monagle specifically praised the actor's&nbsp;
turn as fiction's most iconic vampire, writing,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.360
"In Nicolas Cage's hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.980
Dracula is the perfect marriage between&nbsp;
the rock star and the jilted lover."

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.940
"Exactly, he won't grow to full power. What?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.340
That's so weird. Why would&nbsp;
you phrase it like that?"

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:04.920
As noted previously, the early reviews for&nbsp;
"Renfield" haven't been totally positive. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.760
handful of critics have, in particular,&nbsp;
criticized the film for apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.560
failing to explore its story as much as it&nbsp;
potentially could have. The Seattle Times'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.600
Moira MacDonald said as much in their&nbsp;
negative review of "Renfield," noting,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.680
"Even with its brief running time, the&nbsp;
movie runs out of steam too quickly."

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.520
Elsewhere, Variety critic&nbsp;
Owen Gleiberman took issue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.160
with the thinness of the film's script, writing,

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:34.800
"It's a scattershot lark jam-packed with&nbsp;
'ideas,' none of which really take hold."

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:40.260
Even some of the positive reviews for "Renfield"&nbsp;
have lamented the lightweight nature of the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:45.420
In their ScullyVision review, Dan Scully&nbsp;
gave the horror comedy a fresh rating on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:50.280
Rotten Tomatoes but was also quick to note that&nbsp;
it doesn't quite live up to its own promise.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:55.560
"['Renfield'] proves to be a broadly&nbsp;
pleasing, remarkably safe studio comedy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:00.180
This isn't necessarily a bad thing so much&nbsp;
as it's a case of squandered potential."

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.340
With all this in mind, it seems safe to&nbsp;
say that "Renfield" delivers an enjoyable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.940
if not necessarily outstanding,&nbsp;
experience at the movie theater.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.000
"Focus on your needs."

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.500
Thanks to its mid-April release date,&nbsp;
the film should, in other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:21.420
offer interested viewers a refreshingly&nbsp;
R-rated, bloodsoaked counter to "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:25.680
Super Mario Bros.," which has taken the&nbsp;
moviegoing world by storm this month.

